<article class="env-exercise" id="0FJ6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FJ6">Exercise <span data-tag="0FJ6">111.15.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $f = a_ d x^ d + a_{d - 1} x^{d - 1} + \ldots + a_0 \in R[x]$. (As usual this notation means $a_0, \ldots , a_ d \in R$.) Let $g \in R[x]$. Prove that we can find $N \geq 0$ and $r, q \in R[x]$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  a_ d^ N g = q f + r  \]
</div>
  <p> with $\deg (r) < d$, i.e., for some $c_ i \in R$ we have $r = c_0 + c_1 x + \ldots + c_{d - 1}x^{d - 1}$. </p>
</article>